<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.3 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.3 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 6.3 percent in the week to July 9 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 7.1 percent.</p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			Latest week  Pvs week  Yr-ago week</p>
<p>Notes in circulation  21.81     21.79	20.53</p>
<p>Bankers deposits	 2.58	2.40	 1.92</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
